  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Federal contract obligations in Wyoming total $516M for FY2026 to date. That amount comes from 1,874 awards, with an average award size of $275K, and obligations are up 3.9% year over year. The Department of the Interior is the largest buyer at $309M, followed by the Department of Defense at $77.3M and the Department of Veterans Affairs at $41.1M. Construction and infrastructure work dominate the mix: Water and Sewer Line and Related Structures Construction accounts for $246M and Highway, Street, and Bridge Construction accounts for $62.6M. Record Steel and Construction, Inc. and G.S.E. Construction Company, Inc. are the top two vendors with $129M and $109M, respectively. Other notable vendors include THE ARMORED GROUP LLC at $26.4M and AECOM + TETRA TECH JOINT VENTURE at $22.7M. These figures reflect fiscal year to date obligations and current-year totals are partial.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies drive federal spending in Wyoming?",
        "body": "The Department of the Interior drives federal spending in Wyoming with $309M in obligations. The Department of Defense follows with $77.3M, and the Department of Veterans Affairs contributes $41.1M. Several smaller buyers also show up in the top 10, including the Department of Transportation at $39.1M and the General Services Administration at $26.8M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What sectors and vendors capture most of the work?",
        "body": "Construction-related industries capture the largest share, led by Water and Sewer Line and Related Structures Construction at $246M and Highway, Street, and Bridge Construction at $62.6M. The largest vendors are RECORD STEEL AND CONSTRUCTION, INC. at $129M and G.S.E. CONSTRUCTION COMPANY, INC. at $109M, with THE ARMORED GROUP LLC at $26.4M and AECOM + TETRA TECH JOINT VENTURE at $22.7M also in the top ranks."
      }
    ]
  },
